# ---- Pool image bake debounce (hub only, optional — 30 minutes is the default) ----
# bin/fleet-propagate.sh (*/5) rebakes every pool builder image when a merge
# touches a fleet path, and each bake is a remote Fly build. A burst of merges
# would otherwise start ten of them every five minutes.
#   POOL_IMAGE_MIN_AGE_MIN  minutes a pool image must be old before the lane
#                           rebakes it. Default 30. A pool inside the window is
#                           recorded `debounced` (never a --critical) and marked
#                           dirty; the next tick whose window has expired bakes
#                           it, even when nothing new has merged.
#                           0 = rebake on every propagation, the behaviour
#                           before this knob existed.
#                           An unparseable value logs one line and uses 30.
# Ledger, on the hub: state/fly/<project>.baked-at (epoch of the last bake that
# returned ok) and state/fly/<project>.image-dirty (the sha a debounce skipped).
# --force and the nightly bin/fly-image-refresh.sh ignore this knob and always
# bake. See docs/verification-map/pool-image-debounce.md.
#POOL_IMAGE_MIN_AGE_MIN=30

